{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778561963658,"sessionID":"ses_1e574ee2affes9DYBY0xc4LX9U","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9461eef794d118ec","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"mucosal immune response"},"output":"Found 25 matches\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json:\n  Line 2:   \"body\": \"The textual and logical definition for this term limits IELs to \\\"intestinal epithelium\\\" only, but IELs are found in multiple epithelial tissues - Gastrointestinal tract, Reproductive tract, oral cavity etc... \\n\\n1) Broaden the definition of \\\"intraepithelial lymphocyte\\\"\\n2) Add a specific subclass \\\"intestinal intraepithelial lymphocyte\\\"\\n\\n**Improved textual definition**\\nA tissue-resident lymphocyte located within the epithelial layer of mucosal tissues, particularly within the gastrointestinal, respiratory, and reproductive tracts. Characterised by permanent residency, this cell typically expresses CD103 (ntegrin alpha-E), which binds to E-cadherin on epithelial cells, enabling epithelial retention in both mice and humans. Phenotypically, IEL displays an activated, antigen-experienced state characterised by the constitutive expression of cytotoxic molecules (granzyme B, perforin) and innate-like receptors (such as NKG2D), enabling rapid, localised surveillance and immediate response to epithelial stress.\\n\\n**Add these references (DO NOT replace existing ones)**\\n\\nPMID: [29674648](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29674648/)\\nWIKIPEDIA:Intraepithelial lymphocyte\\n\\n**Logical definition**\\n'mature T cell'\\n and ('located in' some 'epithelium')\\n and ('capable of' some 'mucosal immune response')\\n\\n--- \\n\\n**intestinal intraepithelial lymphocyte**\\n\\n**textual definition**\\nA T cell that is located in the intestinal epithelium and is capable of a mucosal immune response.\\n\\nPMID: [29674648](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29674648/)\\nWIKIPEDIA:Intraepithelial lymphocyte\\n\\n**logical definition**\\n\\nEquivilantTo\\n'mature T cell'\\n and ('located in' some 'intestinal epithelium')\\n and ('capable of' some 'mucosal immune response')\\n\\n**ORCID**\\nhttps://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\\n\\n\",\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/imports/merged_import.owl:\n  Line 24248: # Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0002385> (mucosal immune response)\n\n  Line 24257: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0002385> \"mucosal immune response\")\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/cl-refactored.owl:\n  Line 5885: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"GOC:add\"^^xsd:string) Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"GOC:tfm\"^^xsd:string) Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"ISBN:0781735149\"^^xsd:string) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000801> \"A mature gamma-delta T cell that is found in the columnar epithelium of the gastrointestinal tract. These cells participate in mucosal immune responses.\"^^xsd:string)\n\n  Line 12934: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"GOC:tfm\"^^xsd:string) Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"MP:0008894\"^^xsd:string) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002496> \"A T cell that is located in the intestinal epithelium and is capable of a mucosal immune response.\"^^xsd:string)\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/cl-edit_neg_exp.owl:\n  Line 24686:         <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string\">A mature gamma-delta T cell that is found in the columnar epithelium of the gastrointestinal tract. These